;
; How Poultice files one entry of the care plan in MYRA (poultice_rules.h
; PR5): under the patient, the entry's kind (1 symptom, 2 dose given,
; 3 vital reading), its item (the symptom, the medicine or the vital),
; its day (days since 1970), its minute of the day and the carer who
; logged it, holding its value (a severity, a dose in the plan's unit or a
; reading). The carer is in the key, so two carers' entries for one minute
; are two nodes, both kept. Advisory: the tree is a record, never a
; diagnosis.
^ZXPOULT(patient:i4, kind:i1, item:i4, day:i6, minute:i4, carer:i2) = value:i9!
